    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Jackson Merrill** headlining the offensive unit. Boasting an elite 75.27 efficiency score, **Jackson Merrill** is positioned for a breakout performance against Merrill Kelly; the combination of a favorable 5.37 xERA matchup and the projected #2 lineup spot makes him our highest-ceiling asset. **Jacob Wilson** also warrants significant attention at 69.78, aided by a beneficial wind-out factor and a strong SP matchup against Valdez, while **Gunnar Henderson** (68.29) and **Coby Mayo** (65.57) provide a potent core against Peterson, though both will need to navigate the risk of facing a pitcher who effectively limits our stolen base opportunities.\n\nStrategic lineup construction required a difficult choice at the bench, where **Miguel Vargas** was the most notable exclusion. While **Miguel Vargas** maintained a strong 0.403 xwOBA, his efficiency score of 42.64 was suppressed by a daunting matchup against Sandoval, leaving him just short of displacing **Nolan Schanuel** or **Josh Jung** in today\u2019s configuration. We are also keeping a close eye on the volatile nature of the bottom tier of our lineup: **Liam Hicks** carries a slim 40.73 score, hovering just above our \"Below Floor\" threshold due to a difficult matchup against Miller, while **Josh Lowe** and **Nolan Schanuel** remain high-risk plays against Eovaldi. \n\nManagers should monitor the status of **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill** closely, as both rely on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions; if either shifts down in the order, their efficiency scores will require immediate re-evaluation. While we are heavily prioritizing elite sprint speed to bolster our SB standing, the matchup against the pitching tandem of Eovaldi and Peterson creates a high-variance environment. We remain confident in the upside provided by **Dominic Smith** and **Drake Baldwin** to bridge the production gap should the top of the order face early resistance from their respective opponents.",
